Vault Auditing
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand the importance of audit logging in HashiCorp Vault
Enable and configure audit logging mechanisms in Vault
Generate audit events through various Vault operations
Analyze audit logs to monitor secret access and security events
Interpret audit log entries to track user activities and system events
Implement best practices for audit log management and security
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with HashiCorp Vault concepts from previous labs
Knowledge of JSON format and basic log analysis
Understanding of file permissions and directory structures in Linux
Basic text processing skills using common Linux utilities
